  "_comment": "Furnishing recipes (furniture quality B) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d purpose -> pieces, replacing FurniturePlacer's hardcoded map (which remains the fallback for purposes absent here). `place`: \"wall\" (default; packs along a free wall, facing in) | \"center\" (room centre). `tiers`: which wealth tiers get the piece (absent = every tier); tiers come from the typology's room_program.json `wealth_tier` (croft/longhouse = humble, hall_house/tavern/shops = middling, manor_hall = high). Mount kind (floor/wall/ceiling) is per-TYPE placer data, not recipe data. `count` (int, default 1) places up to N of the piece; `per_area` places one per N floor cells (area-scaled, cap 12; rep 0 required, later reps best-effort). `as`:\"item\" realizes the piece as a pickable ITEM PROP via ItemPropManager (static-first, parented to the structure) instead of a baked template; `item` overrides the item id (default: the type).",
